event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrclcap — mission \\\"greet, tested\\\"\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\n## What was delivered\\n- `src/greet.py`: `greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: two unit tests — a normal name (`greet(\\\"World\\\")`) and\\n  the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\")`).\\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (2 tests, OK).\\n\\n## How it was verified\\n- Dispatched implementation to `dev` (d002); dev committed to its own branch\\n  (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit `d6049f2`) and reported\\n  a passing test run.\\n- Did not trust the report alone: fetched dev's branch\\n  (`refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`), copied it to an isolated directory,\\n  checked out dev's commit, and independently re-ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`, confirming exit 0.\\n- Inspected the diff directly (`git show --stat`, file contents) to confirm\\n  only `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py` were touched, and that the\\n  test file exercises both required cases.\\n- Accepted dev's d002 reply only after this independent verification.\\n- Fast-forward merged dev's accepted commit onto the orchestrator's own branch\\n  (`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`) at `~/subject`, and\\n  re-ran the test suite there to confirm it still passes on that branch.\\n\\n## Criteria check\\nAll three criteria from mission.md are satisfied:\\n1. `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` — done.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string — done.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 — done, verified independently.\\n\\nNothing remains unmet.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

